{"highest":3,"ids":{"tests lens, medium: No test fixture places a concurrent claim note outside the detection window, so a `since` filter that is always zero (or otherwise ignores the epoch boundary) passes all DSRACE-1 assertions. (plugins/claim-coordinator/github-labels/tests/claim-coordinator-unit-test.sh: \"assert_eq \"[DSRACE-1] all concurrent claim notes from the current label epoch are returned (loser when earlier note is on page 2)\" \"false\" \\\"; happens when: Every test fixture places both notes at `2026-01-01T00:00:00Z` or `..00:01Z`, well inside the `_CCGL_RACE_NOTE_AT - 4 * gt` window (a 20-second lookback for `gt=5`). The `select((try (.created_at | fromdateiso8601) // 0) >= \\$s)` filter in `_ccgl_race_note_first_v` would return the same result whether `since` is the computed epoch-relative value or zero; a broken implementation that hardcodes `since=0` passes every DSRACE-1 assertion. DSRACE-1 requires \"all concurrent claim notes from the current label epoch are returned\" — the boundary behavior (a note whose `created_at` is before the detection window is excluded) is not checked by any fixture.; fix: test; ACCEPTED IF: a test fixture exists in which a concurrent claim note whose `created_at` is older than `_CCGL_RACE_NOTE_AT - 4 * ZBUILD_STATUS_COMMENT_GH_TIMEOUT` seconds is present in the notes list, and the assertions confirm that note is excluded from arbitration (the run is not counted as a loser because of a note from a prior claim cycle))":"RLTESTS-1","tests lens, medium: DSRACE-2 names \"first by created_at, then id\" as the ordering rule, but every test fixture uses distinct created_at values; no fixture has two notes with the same created_at and different ids, so the .id secondary sort in `sort_by(.t, .id)` is never the tie-breaker — a broken `sort_by(.t)` (ignoring .id) passes every DSRACE-2 assertion. (plugins/claim-coordinator/github-labels/tests/claim-coordinator-unit-test.sh: \"assert_eq \"[DSRACE-2] loser reply: acquired is false\" \"false\" \\\"; happens when: Two concurrent notes arrive at GitHub within the same one-second slot (GitHub rounds created_at to seconds), so both have identical created_at; the smaller id must win; without a fixture for this case, a sort that drops the id column goes undetected.; fix: test; ACCEPTED IF: a test fixture exists in which two concurrent claim notes have an identical created_at value and different ids, and the assertions confirm that the note with the smaller id is identified as the winner (acquired: true for the lower-id note, acquired: false and race_lost: true for the higher-id note)); the same kind of problem also at: plugins/claim-coordinator/github-labels/tests/claim-coordinator-unit-test.sh | assert_eq \"[DSRACE-2] winner (sole claimant) reply: acquired is true\" \"true\" \\":"RLTESTS-2","tests lens, medium: RQLBL-1 (\"the later run exits without removing the label\") is exercised at the claim.sh layer with a stub coordinator (DSRACE-4), but the coordinator unit tests that run the real plugin.sh loser path (the DSRACE-2 and DSRACE-3 fixtures) never assert that $GHS/labels still contains zbuild:claimed after claim_coordinator_claim returns; an accidental _ccgl_remove_label call in the loser branch of plugin.sh would go undetected by both DSRACE-2 and DSRACE-3. (plugins/claim-coordinator/github-labels/tests/claim-coordinator-unit-test.sh: \"assert_eq \"[DSRACE-1] all concurrent claim notes from the current label epoch are returned (loser when earlier note is on page 2)\" \"false\" \\\"; happens when: A future change adds a label-cleanup call to the loser branch in plugin.sh (e.g. in the _ccgl_race_note_update error path); DSRACE-4 at the claim.sh layer uses a stub and would not see the removal; the coordinator unit tests run real plugin.sh code but check only the PATCH and the reply JSON, not the labels file.; fix: test; ACCEPTED IF: at least one coordinator unit test that exercises the loser path (a concurrent claim note exists whose created_at is earlier than this run's) also asserts that the zbuild:claimed label remains on the issue after claim_coordinator_claim returns); the same kind of problem also at: plugins/claim-coordinator/github-labels/tests/claim-coordinator-unit-test.sh | assert_eq \"[DSRACE-3] the losing run made a PATCH call on its own note (id 99004)\" \"1\" \\":"RLTESTS-3"}}
